# Practical 04 - Property Binding

## Aim

To demonstrate Property Binding in Angular.

## Theory

Property Binding is used to bind a value from the component class to a property of an HTML element.

1. app.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  templateUrl: './app.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./app.component.css']
})
export class AppComponent {

  title = 'Property Binding Example';

  imageUrl = 'https://angular.dev/assets/images/press-kit/angular_icon_gradient.gif';

  imageWidth = 150;

  buttonDisabled = false;
}

2. app.component.html
<div class="container">

  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>

  <h2>Property Binding Example</h2>

  <img [src]="imageUrl" [width]="imageWidth">

  <br><br>

  <button [disabled]="buttonDisabled">
    Click Me
  </button>

</div>

